unit has the Infiltrate special rule (see the main rulebook).</description></rule><rule id="8449-10a3-ffbb-495b" name="Move Through Cover" hidden="false"><description>This unit has the Move Through Cover special rule (see the main rulebook).</description></rule><rule id="73ff-109b-2c1c-4396" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, that enemy has caught the ire of the Votann. Place a Grudge token next to it to denote this effect. Each enemy unit tracks their own Grudge tokens separately, up to a maximum of three per enemy unit. Independent Characters attached to units use the Grudge tokens of the unit they are attached to. If an enemy Independent Character leaves their unit, they gain the same amount of Grudge tokens that their unit had prior. Conversely, if an enemy Independent Character with Grudge tokens attaches themselves to a unit, use the higher of the Grudge token pools between them and discard the other. Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many Grudge tokens the target enemy unit has, their effects incrementally increasing to match the heightened threat of the foe. 1: Leagues of Votann units are Stubborn while engaged with an enemy unit with a Grudge token. 2: Leagues of Votann units suffer Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens. 3: Leagues of Votann units gain the Preferred Enemy special rule against an enemy unit with 3 tokens. In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule><rule id="0fef-7d33-a25d-489c" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A unit composed entirely of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to Run in the shooting phase, always move 3&quot; instead of rolling to determine the distance.</description></rule><rule id="0904-9057-2b8d-409c" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this special rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule><rule id="be31-f53b-3c13-4d3c" name="Mounted Assault" hidden="false"><description>When deploying a unit with this rule that has purchased dedicated transports, you may split the squad into separate units. Split the squad so that each vehicle has its transport capacity as filled as possible. The dedicated transports and the models embarked within them are then considered separate units for all intents and purposes. Any remaining models that cannot embark upon the dedicated transports remain as their own separate unit.</description></rule></rules><costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="60" /></costs></selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="1167-ba92-aad4-16cc" name="Buri Aegnirssen" hidden="false" type="model" collective="false" import="true">
      <comment>Unique. Rebuilt from VOTANN_DEX_REDUX.pdf.</comment>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="925d-6978-e0e0-9685" type="max" field="selections" scope="roster" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="f163-fd49-5737-d499" name="Buri Aegnirssen" hidden="false" typeId="2d6001b0-980e-46d2-bcc2-a9fc60109afd" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="c2b4b061-a0fd-499d-8a3d-6ee52587cbd5">Infantry (Character)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="5ee4ff0b-b244-4670-9d05-91d10f80c32e">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="f6f92f00-8bb1-4afa-8ccb-46310b7dd5e5">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="da036dbb-32c2-430a-9dd5-aa74e0c4f74b">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="3f9ed75c-36cd-4169-9cef-48391bb55cfd">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="17ee558f-3014-4bd2-afc1-b474d8d2b7a8">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="a558b3ef-04d0-440e-a312-bac3255bf592">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="5dff3e7c-e024-4030-a71d-03195ec06ea7">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="4a42059d-12cd-4c1f-a4c7-bb569d13eeea">10</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="b215fe72-dbce-4ad6-89ec-c4bb3962c39d">3+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="e878-9be1-0cd2-4271" name="Independent Character" hidden="false"><description>This model is an Independent Character.</description></rule>
        <rule id="983e-4c57-394b-42ce" name="Rampage" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Rampage special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="35ba-5516-73ae-4645" name="Monster Hunter" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Monster Hunter special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="e96d-f1c9-5f59-4444" name="Hatred (Tyranids)" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Hatred (Tyranids) special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="c19c-18b0-30a4-43d7" name="Thrice Devoured" hidden="false"><description>Whenever Buri Aegnirssen loses his last Wound, roll 2D6. If the combined result is equal to or less than the total number of Grudge token on the battlefield, Buri is not removed as a casualty and lives on with one Wound remaining.</description></rule>
        <rule id="c57b-17ff-252e-47ef" name="Grim Efficiency" hidden="false"><description>After deploying but before rolling to seize the initiative, as long as you have a model with this rule in your army, place a single Grudge Token on an enemy unit.</description></rule>
        <rule id="8c3e-7f6c-58bf-4cf3" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, that enemy has caught the ire of the Votann. Place a Grudge token next to it to denote this effect. Each enemy unit tracks their own Grudge tokens separately, up to a maximum of three per enemy unit. Independent Characters attached to units use the Grudge tokens of the unit they are attached to. If an enemy Independent Character leaves their unit, they gain the same amount of Grudge tokens that their unit had prior. Conversely, if an enemy Independent Character with Grudge tokens attaches themselves to a unit, use the higher of the Grudge token pools between them and discard the other. Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many Grudge tokens the target enemy unit has, their effects incrementally increasing to match the heightened threat of the foe. 1: Leagues of Votann units are Stubborn while engaged with an enemy unit with a Grudge token. 2: Leagues of Votann units suffer Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens. 3: Leagues of Votann units gain the Preferred Enemy special rule against an enemy unit with 3 tokens. In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule>
        <rule id="6e93-a483-fb9e-4e19" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A unit composed entirely of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to Run in the shooting phase, always move 3" instead of rolling to determine the distance.</description></rule>
        <rule id="41df-5e8f-09c7-4eb9" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this special rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule>
        <rule id="6af3-39bb-9fdb-4217" name="Warlord Trait: Warrior Lord" hidden="false"><description>When fielded as your Warlord, Buri Aegnirssen has the Warrior Lord warlord trait (the Warlord and any unit they join gain the Monster Hunter and Furious Charge special rules) instead of rolling to generate one.</description></rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks><categoryLink id="404c-95d8-c0dd-49e3" name="HQ" hidden="false" targetId="848a6ff2-0def-4c72-8433-ff7da70e6bc7" primary="true" /></categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="7d72-4ade-b6e4-66e0" name="Bane, the Darkstar Spear" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true"><constraints><constraint id="2092-2eda-29e2-4bd2" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /><constraint id="d64f-820f-3137-4e6c" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><profiles><profile id="f83a-ca50-3142-4834" name="Bane, the Darkstar Spear" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">-</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">User</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Melee, Two-handed, Fleshbane, Specialist Weapon, Darkstar</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile></profiles><rules><rule id="9c21-217b-d60a-4ff4" name="Darkstar" hidden="false"><description>Wounds caused by this weapon cannot be negated by the Feel No Pain special rule.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="f296-ad62-7446-4c9c" name="Armour of Ugnÿr" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true"><constraints><constraint id="a1ab-fb6a-ba91-4eb9" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /><constraint id="e3b4-ff29-23c9-477c" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><rules><rule id="db89-e244-b1ff-4c97" name="Armour of Ugnÿr" hidden="false"><description>The wearer is immune to the effects of the Fleshbane and Poisoned special rules. If as a result the attack has no strength value, it wounds on a To Wound roll of a 6.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="cc47-1aa2-3cf2-c685" name="Warlord" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true">
