    <selectionEntry id="54bc-9952-76d7-d1ac" name="Memnyr Strategist" hidden="false" type="model" collective="false" import="true">
      <comment>Retinue character. Rebuilt from VOTANN_DEX_REDUX.pdf.</comment><modifiers><modifier type="increment" field="a5b6-675e-141e-3eb2" value="1"><repeats><repeat field="selections" scope="force" childId="848a6ff2-0def-4c72-8433-ff7da70e6bc7" value="1" repeats="1" roundUp="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></repeats></modifier><modifier type="increment" field="a5b6-675e-141e-3eb2" value="-1"><repeats><repeat field="selections" scope="force" childId="878d-e170-c09f-89b4" value="1" repeats="1" roundUp="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></repeats></modifier></modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="a5b6-675e-141e-3eb2" type="max" field="selections" scope="force" value="0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="8a7f-fdd8-650d-9f96" name="Memnyr Strategist" hidden="false" typeId="2d6001b0-980e-46d2-bcc2-a9fc60109afd" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="c2b4b061-a0fd-499d-8a3d-6ee52587cbd5">Infantry (Character)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="5ee4ff0b-b244-4670-9d05-91d10f80c32e">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="f6f92f00-8bb1-4afa-8ccb-46310b7dd5e5">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="da036dbb-32c2-430a-9dd5-aa74e0c4f74b">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="3f9ed75c-36cd-4169-9cef-48391bb55cfd">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="17ee558f-3014-4bd2-afc1-b474d8d2b7a8">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="a558b3ef-04d0-440e-a312-bac3255bf592">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="5dff3e7c-e024-4030-a71d-03195ec06ea7">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="4a42059d-12cd-4c1f-a4c7-bb569d13eeea">9</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="b215fe72-dbce-4ad6-89ec-c4bb3962c39d">4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="1807-de74-0b72-4e31" name="Retinue" hidden="false"><description>Characters with this rule do not take up a force organization slot. Instead, for every HQ taken, you may take one Character with this rule. What units these Characters may deploy within are indicated on their Datasheet. Only a single model with this rule may be attached to the same unit, and a model with this rule may not be nominated as your warlord. A Memnyr Strategist may be deployed joining a unit of Hearthkyn Warriors or Ironkin Steeljacks.</description></rule>
        <rule id="0289-0e85-b6e2-423f" name="Outflank" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Outflank special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="49ec-bfb0-badb-4328" name="Acute Senses" hidden="false"><description>This model has the Acute Senses special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="0b3c-64c8-2da8-49fa" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, that enemy has caught the ire of the Votann. Place a Grudge token next to it to denote this effect. Each enemy unit tracks their own Grudge tokens separately, up to a maximum of three per enemy unit. Independent Characters attached to units use the Grudge tokens of the unit they are attached to. If an enemy Independent Character leaves their unit, they gain the same amount of Grudge tokens that their unit had prior. Conversely, if an enemy Independent Character with Grudge tokens attaches themselves to a unit, use the higher of the Grudge token pools between them and discard the other. Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many Grudge tokens the target enemy unit has, their effects incrementally increasing to match the heightened threat of the foe. 1: Leagues of Votann units are Stubborn while engaged with an enemy unit with a Grudge token. 2: Leagues of Votann units suffer Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens. 3: Leagues of Votann units gain the Preferred Enemy special rule against an enemy unit with 3 tokens. In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule>
        <rule id="d982-350a-d8d5-42af" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A unit composed entirely of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to Run in the shooting phase, always move 3" instead of rolling to determine the distance.</description></rule>
        <rule id="3993-fd35-5956-4afd" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this special rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks><categoryLink id="2974-045d-97e8-44a2" name="No Force Org Slot" hidden="false" targetId="ff36a6f3-19bf-4f48-8956-adacfd28fe74" primary="true" /></categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="43d2-26cb-f275-4269" name="Bolt Pistol" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true"><constraints><constraint id="53c1-26bc-db65-455b" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /><constraint id="e1ac-b582-bfc0-4e0c" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><profiles><profile id="adf8-7a0c-b5be-4374" name="Bolt Pistol" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">12"</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Pistol 1</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile></profiles></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="ade0-0488-856d-4322" name="Kognitâar Mantle" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true"><constraints><constraint id="146a-54ef-8aad-4a92" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /><constraint id="cba9-de7e-ccaf-4c56" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><rules><rule id="4dae-2c1d-d809-4611" name="Kognitâar Mantle" hidden="false"><description>At the start of each turn that a model equipped with a Kognitâar Mantle is on the battlefield, that model may take a leadership test. If passed, select from one of the following special rules to either grant to a friendly unit until the start of your next turn: Counter Attack, Tank Hunter, Split Fire. If the Leadership test is failed, the model equipped with a Kognitâar Mantle and their unit Go to Ground as they await for the computational overload to dissipate.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="75" /></costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="878d-e170-c09f-89b4" name="Arkanyst Evaluator" hidden="false" type="model" collective="false" import="true">
      <comment>Retinue character. Rebuilt from VOTANN_DEX_REDUX.pdf.</comment><modifiers><modifier type="increment" field="bb5e-a1b6-56a6-e3d8" value="1"><repeats><repeat field="selections" scope="force" childId="848a6ff2-0def-4c72-8433-ff7da70e6bc7" value="1" repeats="1" roundUp="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></repeats></modifier><modifier type="increment" field="bb5e-a1b6-56a6-e3d8" value="-1"><repeats><repeat field="selections" scope="force" childId="54bc-9952-76d7-d1ac" value="1" repeats="1" roundUp="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></repeats></modifier></modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="bb5e-a1b6-56a6-e3d8" type="max" field="selections" scope="force" value="0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="dfbe-4619-7e67-1ad9" name="Arkanyst Evaluator" hidden="false" typeId="2d6001b0-980e-46d2-bcc2-a9fc60109afd" typeName="Unit">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Unit Type" typeId="c2b4b061-a0fd-499d-8a3d-6ee52587cbd5">Infantry (Character)</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="5ee4ff0b-b244-4670-9d05-91d10f80c32e">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="f6f92f00-8bb1-4afa-8ccb-46310b7dd5e5">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="da036dbb-32c2-430a-9dd5-aa74e0c4f74b">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="3f9ed75c-36cd-4169-9cef-48391bb55cfd">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="17ee558f-3014-4bd2-afc1-b474d8d2b7a8">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="a558b3ef-04d0-440e-a312-bac3255bf592">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="5dff3e7c-e024-4030-a71d-03195ec06ea7">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="4a42059d-12cd-4c1f-a4c7-bb569d13eeea">8</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Save" typeId="b215fe72-dbce-4ad6-89ec-c4bb3962c39d">4+</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="804d-abfb-7ebf-4a25" name="Experimental Munitions" hidden="false"><description>Boltguns, Bolt Pistols, and Heavy Bolters in a unit with a model with this rule gain the Poisoned (4+) special rule.</description></rule>
        <rule id="4c60-40c2-a105-47db" name="Retinue" hidden="false"><description>Characters with this rule do not take up a force organization slot. Instead, for every HQ taken, you may take one Character with this rule. What units these Characters may deploy within are indicated on their Datasheet. Only a single model with this rule may be attached to the same unit, and a model with this rule may not be nominated as your warlord. An Arkanyst Evaluator may be deployed joining a unit of Hearthkyn Warriors or Brôkhyr Thunderkyn.</description></rule>
        <rule id="7389-3641-6bde-4645" name="Eye of the Ancestors" hidden="false"><description>Whenever an enemy destroys one of your units or slays a model with the character unit subtype in a challenge, that enemy has caught the ire of the Votann. Place a Grudge token next to it to denote this effect. Each enemy unit tracks their own Grudge tokens separately, up to a maximum of three per enemy unit. Independent Characters attached to units use the Grudge tokens of the unit they are attached to. If an enemy Independent Character leaves their unit, they gain the same amount of Grudge tokens that their unit had prior. Conversely, if an enemy Independent Character with Grudge tokens attaches themselves to a unit, use the higher of the Grudge token pools between them and discard the other. Your Leagues of Votann units gain stacking bonuses depending on how many Grudge tokens the target enemy unit has, their effects incrementally increasing to match the heightened threat of the foe. 1: Leagues of Votann units are Stubborn while engaged with an enemy unit with a Grudge token. 2: Leagues of Votann units suffer Hatred against an enemy unit with 2 tokens. 3: Leagues of Votann units gain the Preferred Enemy special rule against an enemy unit with 3 tokens. In addition, characters with this rule cannot refuse challenges. If an enemy issues a challenge, a character model with this rule must accept the challenge.</description></rule>
        <rule id="f8bb-33d4-2380-4e9b" name="Steady Advance" hidden="false"><description>A unit composed entirely of models with this rule do not count as having moved while in the shooting phase. Whenever a unit with this rule declares to Run in the shooting phase, always move 3" instead of rolling to determine the distance.</description></rule>
        <rule id="a3df-443a-3b2c-4258" name="Void Armour" hidden="false"><description>Models with this special rule automatically pass Dangerous Terrain tests. In addition, vehicles with this rule count as having Extra Armour.</description></rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks><categoryLink id="b2e6-47bf-1771-4ee6" name="No Force Org Slot" hidden="false" targetId="ff36a6f3-19bf-4f48-8956-adacfd28fe74" primary="true" /></categoryLinks>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="39e4-1a8e-79fb-43c9" name="Transmatter Inverter" hidden="false" type="upgrade" collective="false" import="true"><constraints><constraint id="2bbb-d59a-8899-4826" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /><constraint id="46fe-8ed0-582f-4773" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" /></constraints><profiles><profile id="1d1f-aa08-c3c4-4335" name="Transmatter Inverter" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48" typeName="Weapon">
